           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Jan</span>
            <span class="day">6</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/agile/" title="View all posts in Agile" rel="category tag">Agile</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/coaching/" title="View all posts in Coaching" rel="category tag">Coaching</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/craftsmanship/" title="View all posts in Craftsmanship" rel="category tag">Craftsmanship</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/scrum/" title="View all posts in Scrum" rel="category tag">Scrum</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/training/" title="View all posts in Training" rel="category tag">Training</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2011/01/rules-of-the-game-effective-group-discussion/#comments" class="comments"  title="Comment on Rules of the Game: Effective Group Discussion"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="848 http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2011/01/rules-of-the-game-effective-group-discussion/">2 Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>Meetings are hard.&#160; They can easily suck the life out of your day, week, or *gasp* job.&#160; Let pain be your guide. (Thanks @coreyhaines) I recently had to work through a mountain of feedback data provided by a limited product release.&#160; User Experience experts, random individuals, and customers known for their willingness to provide quality [...]</p>

